							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">Also, UoP also just changed Guild Leader and several officers out, or so I was told.&nbsp; Thrashhash is now leading UOP, Migatol has finally let those reigns go.&nbsp; Too bad it didnt happen a year ago IMO.&nbsp; There are some good people in that guild who care a ton about the guild and its progress, but many of them have been forced or shoved to RoS while others have had to sit on the sidelines while the current &quot;Buddy System of Officers&quot; sat around and spun circles for nearly a year now.</div><br />Posted by Mendolok November 24, 2004, 12:51:00 at here:<br /><br /><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=320.1515" target="_blank">http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=320.1515</a><br /><br />&nbsp;<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Smileys/Rodcet/wtf1.gif" alt="WTF" border="0" /><br /><br />What exactly is the &quot;Buddy System of Officers&quot; you are talking about Mendolok?&nbsp; Are you saying that the great leaders of UoP like Kriptic, Graceystorm, etc.&nbsp; &quot;forced or shoved&quot; many UoP members to RoS because of their lack of leadership and inaction?&nbsp; Are you suggesting those, including myself, who left UoP for RoS had a good reasons for doing so and it could have been avoided had their been competent leadership?&nbsp; I&#039;m confused bro, help me out here.<br /><br />P.S.&nbsp; I will give you credit for the mock Slayyerr application.&nbsp; While I like Slayyerr, that&#039;s pretty creative and funny.
